40. CRITICAL DESIGN PRINCIPLES
==================================================

Follow these principles throughout development:

1. AI recommends. Humans approve.

2. Mapping confidence is NOT the same as data quality.

3. Validation must be deterministic.

4. Keep AI logic separate from validation logic.

5. Keep file storage replaceable.

6. Keep LLM provider replaceable.

7. Keep authentication replaceable.

8. Make migration objects configuration-driven.

9. Approved mappings and transformation rules must be versioned.

10. Every important decision should be auditable.

11. Never overwrite historical results.

12. Excel is an output/report, not the application's primary datastore.

13. PostgreSQL is the authoritative application database.

14. Reference data should come from configurable reference tables.

15. Business users must be able to override AI recommendations.

16. Every override should be auditable.

17. Do not send unnecessary source data to the LLM. Prefer metadata and limited representative samples.

18. Do not expose secrets or sensitive information in logs.


